Āma. Ayaṃ pāṭho Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (VRI) potthake Dhammapada 361. gāthāyaṃ evaṃ dissati:

> Kāyena saṃvaro sādhu, sādhu vācāya saṃvaro;  
> Manasā saṃvaro sādhu, sādhu sabbattha saṃvaro;  
> Sabbattha saṃvuto bhikkhu, sabbadukkhā pamuccati.

Yesaṃ sannicayo natthi, ye pariññātabhojanā;  
suññato animitto ca, vimokkho yesaṃ gocaro;  
ākāse sakuntānaṃ, padaṃ tesaṃ durannayaṃ.

Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (VRI) edition:

> “Appampi ce saṃhita bhāsamāno, dhammassa hoti anudhammacārī;  
> **rāgañca dosañca pahāya mohaṃ, sammappajāno suvimuttacitto;  
> anupādiyāno idha vā huraṃ vā, sa bhāgavā sāmaññassa hoti.**”

**Dhammapada 74** (*Bālavagga*), not Dhammapada 184. In the Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (VRI) text, the verse is:

> “Mam’eva kata maññantu, gihīpabbajitā ubho;  
> Mam’eva ativasā assu, kiccākiccesu kismici;  
> Iti bālassa saṅkappo, icchā māno ca vaḍḍhati.”

Dhammapada 184 begins **“Khantī paramaṃ tapo titikkhā…”**.

Dhammapada 337 (Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana/VRI):

**Tasmā piyaṃ na kayirātha, piyāpāyo hi pāpako;  
Ganthā tesaṃ na vijjanti, yesaṃ natthi piyāppiyaṃ.**

Āma. Ayaṃ pāṭho Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (VRI) Tipiṭake **Dhammapada, Taṇhāvaggo, gāthā 337**-ti dissati:

> Taṃ vo vadāmi bhaddaṃ vo, yāvantettha samāgatā;  
> Taṇhāya mūlaṃ khaṇatha, usīratthova bīraṇaṃ;  
> Mā vo naḷaṃva sotova, māro bhañji punappunaṃ.

Tasmā tumhākaṃ uddhaṭo pāṭho VRI-pāṭhena sameti.

Dhammapada 8:

**Appamādarato bhikkhu, pamāde bhayadassivā;  
Saṃyojanaṃ aṇuṃ thūlaṃ, ḍahaṃ aggīva gacchatī ti.**

“**Na tāvatā dhammadharo, yāvatā bahu bhāsati;  
Yo ca appampi sutvāna, dhammaṃ kāyena passati;  
Sa ve dhammadharo hoti, yo dhammaṃ nappamajjati.**”

— *Dhammapada* 259 (Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana edition)

Dhammapada 106, na 184:

> Māse māse sahassena, yo yajetha sataṃ samaṃ;  
> Ekañca bhāvitattānaṃ, muhuttamapi pūjaye;  
> Sāyeva pūjanā seyyo, yañce vassasataṃ hutaṃ.

Āma, ayaṃ pāṭho Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (VRI) potthake Dhammapadassa Paṇḍitavagge (76–77) āgato. VRI likhitaṃ sandhāya, pāṭho pana:

“Nidhīnaṃva pavattāraṃ, yaṃ passe vajjadassinaṃ;  
Niggayhavādiṃ medhāviṃ, tādisaṃ paṇḍitaṃ bhaje;  
Tādisaṃ bhajamānassa, seyyo hoti na pāpiyo.”

Iti.

Dhammapada 184 Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (VRI) potthake:

**Khantī paramaṃ tapo titikkhā, nibbānaṃ paramaṃ vadanti buddhā;  
Na hi pabbajito parūpaghātī, samaṇo hoti paraṃ viheṭhayanto.**

Yassāsavā parikkhīṇā, āhāre ca anissito;
Suññato animitto ca, vimokkho yassa gocaro;
Ākāse va sakuntānaṃ, padaṃ tassa durannayaṃ.

310. Abrahmacariyasevanā ca, parassa dārānañca atikkamena;  
musāvādo ca pāṇātipāto ca, surāmerayapānañca;  
pañca dhammā imaṃ lokaṃ, apāyaṃ upapajjare.

Āma, **ayaṃ pāṭho Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (VRI) edisiyāyaṃ dissati**. Dhammapade, Arahantavagge (Dhp 93) evaṃ pāṭho:

> Yassāsavā parikkhīṇā, āhāre ca anissito;  
> Suññato animitto ca, vimokkho yassa gocaro;  
> Ākāse va sakuntānaṃ, padaṃ tassa durannayaṃ.

Padacchedo ca sandhi ca edisiyā anurūpā: *suññato animitto ca* ti *suññato animitto ca*; *ākāse va* ti *ākāse iva*.

**Dhammapada 108 — Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (VRI)**

Māse māse sahassena, yo yajetha sataṃ samaṃ;  
Ekañca bhāvitattānaṃ, muhuttamapi pūjaye;  
Sāyeva pūjanā seyyo, yañce vassasataṃ hutaṃ.

Attanāva kataṁ pāpaṁ, attanā saṅkilissati;  
attanā akataṁ pāpaṁ, attanāva visujjhati.  
Suddhī asuddhi paccattaṁ, nāñño aññaṁ visodhaye.

Attanā hi kataṃ pāpaṃ, attanā saṃkilissati;  
Attanā akataṃ pāpaṃ, attanāva visujjhati.  
Suddhī asuddhi paccattaṃ, nāñño aññaṃ visodhaye.

Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (VRI) Dhammapada 165:

**Attanā hi kataṃ pāpaṃ, attanā saṃkilissati;  
attanā akataṃ pāpaṃ, attanāva visujjhati;  
suddhī asuddhi paccattaṃ, nāñño aññaṃ visodhaye.**

Na Dhammapada 184.

Duppabbajjaṃ durabhiramaṃ durāvāsā gharā dukhā,
Dukkhosamānasaṃvāso dukkhānupatitaddhagū;
Tasmā na caddhagū siyā na ca dukkhānupatito siyā.

No. VRI Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana does not give that wording as a single passage. It combines two verses from the Dhammapada, **Bhikkhuvagga 302–303**, and alters the wording:

> **Duppabbajjaṃ durabhiramaṃ, durāvāsā gharā dukhā;  
> Dukkho’samānasaṃvāso, dukkhānupatitaddhagū;  
> Tasmā na caddhagū siyā, na ca dukkhānupatito siyā.**

The VRI text has **dukkho … saṃvāso** (not *dukkhosamānasaṃvāso*) and, in the next verse, **na ca addhagū siyā** (not *na caddhagū siyā*).
